wikipedia_extract: Isuzu (五十鈴) was the second of six vessels in the Nagara class of
  light cruisers, and like other vessels of her class, she was intended for use as
  the flagship of a destroyer flotilla. She was named after the Isuzu River, near
  Ise Shrine in the Chūbu region of Japan.  She saw action during World War II in
  the Battle of Hong Kong and in the Solomon Islands campaign, and the Battle of Leyte
  Gulf before being sunk by American submarines in the Netherlands East Indies in
  April 1945.
